{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246130",
      "title": "Why We Need A Special Project Setup",
      "sourceHash": "a742b9b16d293fbb4de0d233639e2e17d027b028ba79a3affb81c943749a343f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "So React has a lot of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "and you learned about a lot of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "throughout this course, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "But React also has some features that are part of React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "but that you can't use in every React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 20.823,
          "en": "as strange as that might sound.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 26.69,
          "en": "And specifically I'm talking about React Server Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "Server Actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 33.98,
          "en": "and the use hook when used in conjunction with Promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "These are features which can't just be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "in every React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 44.52,
          "en": "Instead, these features require special project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.52,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "setups or special libraries that must be installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 50.85,
          "en": "They're not supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.85,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "by standard Vanilla React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "like the ones you can create with Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "though these are very popular projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "so therefore, indeed most React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 66.453,
          "en": "can't use these features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "But you can thanks to this section in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "and thanks to projects like Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 78.663,
          "en": "which give you a setup that do unlock these features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 83.763,
          "en": "But why are they so hard to use in the first place?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.8,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "Certain React features like React server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "and server actions can't be used in standard vanilla React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 98.25,
          "en": "projects because they actually involve code that needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.25,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "to run on the server side, not just in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "And with standard React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "you have just the browser side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "So a project setup is needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "that actually splits the code automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.14,
          "en": "kind of into two main packages, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.14,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "One package that's meant to never execute in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 125.07300000000001,
          "en": "and one package that is meant to run there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "And then the project also must provide a server site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "environment for that code to run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "that shouldn't run in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "That's why a special setup is needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 139.59,
          "en": "because the code needs to be split",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.59,
          "end": 142.863,
          "en": "because not all features work in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 146.37,
          "en": "Now, one project setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.37,
          "end": 151.37,
          "en": "that does support these features would be a next.js project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "like the one we used in the previous course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 160.17000000000002,
          "en": "Because next.js is a framework that builds up on React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.17000000000002,
          "end": 162.75,
          "en": "and that adds many features to React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.75,
          "end": 166.62,
          "en": "But one feature it adds is that it does set up a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.62,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "where the code is split, as I just described it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "and where there is an environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 174.393,
          "en": "for the server side code to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "That's why attached to this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 180.42,
          "en": "you find a new next.js project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 180.42,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "a very simple one, which we'll use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 186.75,
          "en": "to dive into these core concepts here and to explore them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.75,
          "end": 190.74,
          "en": "And that's also why it helps if you at least started with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 190.74,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "that next.js course section so that you understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 197.523,
          "en": "the structure of such a next.js project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 201.12,
          "en": "Though it isn't too difficult in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.12,
          "end": 205.32,
          "en": "in next.js projects, you can set up page.js files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.32,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "to define different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "for your multi-page server rendered React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 214.74,
          "en": "because next.js is a full stack react framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "and you can then use components in these pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 219.69,
          "en": "to compose your user interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.69,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "You learn all the details about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "in that previous section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "In this section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 228.51,
          "en": "we'll actually only work on one page anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 231.81,
          "en": "So you don't need to know about any advanced next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 234.3,
          "en": "features or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "Once you downloaded this attached project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "you simply have to run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 240.9,
          "en": "to install all the dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.9,
          "end": 242.91,
          "en": "and you can then start the development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.91,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "by running npm run dev.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 246.36,
          "en": "And with that out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.36,
          "end": 250.8,
          "en": "we're now ready to dive into these special React features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.8,
          "end": 252.55,
          "en": "if you want to call them like this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}